en:
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Interesting_Ethereals_Horde:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Find Interesting Ethereals Inside the Auction House!</h1><br/>
<p>You can find Ameer Greatluck, Tiraxis, Marazz, and Courier Malik inside any Auction House!<br/><br/>
These Ethereals offer a variety of essential services. Talk to each of them to see what they offer.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\tiraxis1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Tiraxis runs the Ethereal Bazaar!</h1><br/>
<p>Tiraxis runs the Ethereal Bazaar, offering exclusive cosmetic items that randomly rotate and have a limited stock, making these appearances hyper exclusive.<br/><br/>
You can also redeem Bazaar Tokens for Heirlooms, Vanity Collection items like the Book of Ascension, convenience items like Potions of Experience, Stones of Retreat and more from Tiraxis!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\ameer1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Ameer Greatluck Offers Recovery Services!</h1><br/>
<p>You can also open up Recovery Services anytime by clicking Help Request Red Question Mark in your options menu.<br/><br/>
Recovery Services allow you to restore deleted, disenchanted or vendored items! Restore deleted characters and more!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\malik1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Send Unbound Vanity Items to Seasonal Realms with Malik!</h1><br/>
<p>Courier Malik allows you to send Unbound Vanity Collection items from the Area 52 Realm to Seasonal Realms.<br/><br/>
These transferred items are added directly to your collection on the Seasonal Realm.<br/><br/>
You will not receive them in the mail, meaning they are not tradable when transferred.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\3_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Find and use an Enchanting Altar!</h1><br/>
<p>Enchanting Altars can almost always be found in your Capital City outside of the Auction House. Ask nearby players to summon a |cffe6cc80|Hitem:1903513|h[Mystic Enchanting Altar]|h|r if one isn't up!<br/><br/>
Permanent Enchanting Altars can be found in the world. Open your World Map and look for the purple Altar icon to discover their locations. </p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\3_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Obtain an Untarnished Mystic Scroll.</h1><br/>
<p>Interact with an Enchanting Altar: <br/>
•Select the Scrolls Tab<br/>
•Select Obtain Untarnished Mystic Scroll<br/>
•Click Obtain. This costs 10 silver.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\3_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Reforge your Untarnished Mystic Scroll.</h1><br/>
<p>Reforging rerolls the Mystic Enchant contained on your Mystic Scroll.<br/><br/>
You can reforge the same scroll until you find a Mystic Enhant you like. Each reforge costs a Mystic Rune. If you run out of Mystic Runes it will consume gold!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Mystic_Extracts_and_Reforging_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Keep Reforging until you earn a Mystic Extract!</h1><br/>
<p>You gain experience towards your Mystic Enchanting level each time you reforge. Gaining a new Mystic Enchanting level grants you a Mystic Extract.<br/><br/>
Make sure to keep Mystic Enchants you like. You can always obtain a new Untarnished Scroll to keep reforging.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\4_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Save a Mystic Enchant to your Enchant Collection</h1><br/>
<p>Extract a Mystic Enchant from a Mystic Scroll to permanently add it to your Enchant Collection. This collection is realm wide!<br/><br/>
Saving enchants to your collection requires a Mystic Extract.<br/><br/>
Use an Enchanting Altar, click the Scrolls Tab, the click Save to Collection on the Mystic Enchant you want to permanently save.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Mystic_Enchant_Collection_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Collect Mystic Enchants that empower your spells!</h1><br/>
<p>There is no limit to how many Extracts you can earn or Mystic Enchants you can collect!<br/><br/>
You can find Mystic Enchants that empower your current spells and archetype by reforging Mystic Scrolls or buying them from the Auction House.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\6_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Change Your Look with Transmog!</h1><br/>
<p>Transmogrification (commonly known as “mogging”) is a cosmetic system using the equipment saved in the player’s Wardrobe to overwrite the visuals of your equipped gear.<br/><br/>
When transmogging, only the appearance of your equipment changes, not the stats. This way you get the freedom to change your look without losing any of your power!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\6_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Classless Heroes Can Transmog All Types of Gear!</h1><br/>
<p>On a classless server, you have the freedom to assign any gear to its associating slot, regardless of its armor or weapon type, so you can fulfill your hero’s fantasy and look exactly the way you want to!<br/><br/>
To preview your saved cosmetics, open the Wardrobe tab in Character Advancement. In this menu, you can find various ways to customize your character, going so far as to even change shapeshift forms with Incarnations, or the very spells you cast to create your unique hero!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\6_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Preview Your Collection in the Wardrobe</h1><br/>
<p>To transmog, go to the “Items” tab in the upper menu. Use filters or the search bar to find a specific piece of gear you love, or browse each armor slot individually by clicking its icon.<br/><br/>
In this menu, you can preview all of the currently available gear in the game, but it's up to you to collect them and learn their appearance for yourself!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\6_4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Let’s Mog!</h1><br/>
<p>Click on a piece of gear to select it for transmog and the preview of your character in the left menu will update with your selection.<br/><br/>
To save your transmog, click the Apply button at the top. Transmogging is never permanent, so if you change your mind later you can always Right Click an item to revert it back to its original appearance.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\6_5:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Transmog is Saved to the Gear Slot, Not the Equipment Itself!</h1><br/>
<p>To make Transmog as convenient as possible, your new cosmetic is saved to your equipment slot, not the piece of gear itself!<br/><br/>
This allows you the freedom to change your gear without losing your preferred appearance!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\6_6:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Look Awesome, Play Awesome!</h1><br/>
<p>You can perfect your hero’s looks at any time, and from anywhere, with the Wardrobe menu!<br/><br/>
The Wardrobe is your hub for ultimate customization of your character. Mix and match with various equipment, change your shapeshift form, or even find matching armor sets with the upper tabs. There is no limit to what you can do!<br/><br/>
And the best part… it’s all free! There is no cost to change your appearance, you can customize your character as many times as you like without restriction!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\pvepower1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">PvE Power Increases Damage, Healing, and Survivability!</h1><br/>
<p>You can view your PvE Power in your Character Sheet.<br/><br/>
PvE Power is only active at max level and is critical to progressing through end-game PvE content on Ascension.<br/><br/>
PvE Power does not affect other players in PvP! It is only active against creatures.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\pvepower2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Gear Obtained from Dungeons and Raids has PvE Power!</h1><br/>
<p>Gear obtained from max level PvE content has PvE power. This includes Bind on Equip gear.<br/><br/>
Acquire a set of PvE gear by queuing for Dungeons, Call Board Daily Quests, The Manastorm, and through the Auction House (just add "pve" to your search).</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\pvppower1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">PvP Power is Your Most Important PvP Stat!</h1><br/>
<p>PvP Power increases your damage dealt to players and reduces the damage you take from players!<br/><br/>
Healers deal increased healing and absoption in Arenas and Battlegrounds.<br/><br/>
While in the High-Risk Open World PvP Power increases your damage dealt to creatures and reduces your damage taken from creatures.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\pvppower2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Bloodforged, Honor, and Arena Gear Has PvP Power.</h1><br/>
<p>Reaching max PvP power is the most important thing you can do to get better at PvP.<br/><br/>
Acquire a set of PvP gear from Honor Vendors or on the Auction House by searching for "PvP" or "Bloodforged."<br/><br/>
Taking Soulbound PvE gear into PvP will put you at a disadvantage against players in PvP gear.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\pvppower3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">PvP Power Is Only Active at Max Level.</h1><br/>
<p>PvP Power exists on all max level PvP gear. It is not used while leveling.<br/><br/>
You can increase your PvP Power before reaching max level, but you will not gain benefits from it until max level.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\pvppower4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Bloodforge Soulbound Gear into PvP Gear!</h1><br/>
<p>You can Bloodforge Soulbound gear by buying a |cffe6cc80|Hitem:777999|h[Bloody Jar]|h|r from Nozdormu. This cannot be undone!<br/><br/>
Bloodforging Soulbound Honor or Arena gear will reduce their stats, so you should only do so if you want to trade or sell the item!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\15_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Choose Your Raiding Difficulty!</h1><br/>
<p>Normal Raids allow for mistakes and are perfect for practicing fight mechanics without high pressure.<br/><br/>
Right-click your character portrait to set your Raid Difficulty.<br/><br/>
You can complete Normal Raids with beginner gear and builds. They are often advertised in Global Chat and are designed for pickup groups, offering Epic Gear rewards!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\15_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Normal Raids Require No Attunements or Keys!</h1><br/>
<p>Normal Raids are immediately accessible—you can enter them right now!<br/><br/>
There are no attunements, quests, keys, or other prerequisites before entering a Normal Difficulty Raid.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\normalraids2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Raids Adapt to 10-25 Players</h1><br/>
<p>Normal Raids are entry-level PvE content that adapt their difficulty to your raid size, requiring at least 10 players and allowing up to 25.<br/><br/>
They drop more loot and are easier to complete with more players!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\15_4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Experience Loot Lockouts Instead of Raid Locks</h1><br/>
<p>You are not locked to a Raid ID on Ascension. You can join as many raids as you want but are only eligible to loot each boss once.<br/><br/>
This means you can join an in-progress raid and return later for bosses you missed.<br/><br/>
If you need to leave or your raid disbands, you can join a new one and still get loot from any boss you have not already defeated!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\mythicdungeons1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Complete a Mythic Dungeon!</h1><br/>
<p>Open the Dungeon Finder and queue for a Random Mythic Dungeon or select a specific one under Specific Dungeons.<br/><br/>
Mythic Dungeons are more challenging than Heroic Dungeons and offer higher item level gear rewards!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\mythicdungeons2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Defeat the Final Boss to Earn a Mythic Keystone!</h1><br/>
<p>Defeating the final boss of a Mythic Dungeon awards a Mythic Keystone Cache.<br/><br/>
These Keystones allow you to join Mythic+ Dungeons, taking on greater challenges for even more powerful rewards.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\MythicPlus_Dungeon:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Challenge Mythic+ Dungeons!</h1><br/>
<p>Mythic+ Dungeons are timed versions of your favorite dungeons with added twists.<br/><br/>
Enemies are augmented with Affixes that increase difficulty and challenge you in new ways.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Group_Finder:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Form a Group for Mythic+ Dungeons</h1><br/>
<p>You cannot queue for Mythic+ Dungeons using the Dungeon Finder.<br/><br/>
Gather a group of 1 Tank, 1 Healer, and 3 Damage Dealers by inviting players from Guild Chat or Global Chat.<br/><br/>
Travel to the dungeon entrance together.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Keystone_Start:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Begin Your Mythic+ Dungeon!</h1><br/>
<p>Once inside the dungeon, the group leader can use a Mythic Keystone to start the Mythic+ run.<br/><br/>
Use a Stone of Retreat or the First-Class Experimental Teleporter to reach the dungeon quickly.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\19_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Ascended Raiding. Ascended Mechanics. Ascended Loot.</h1><br/>
<p>Ascended Raiding is the ultimate PvE challenge on Ascension and drops the strongest obtainable gear for each Tier!<br/><br/>
Bosses deal more damage, are more durable, and have new challenging mechanics unique to Ascended difficulty.<br/><br/>
Ascended Raids are designed for Players with optimized builds, gear, a coordinate group, and a strong knowledge of the Raid.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\19_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Ascended Raids Should Not Be Attempted with PvP Gear!</h1><br/>
<p>Wearing Bloodforged or PvP gear in Ascended Raids will apply the Bloody debuff to you, massively reducing your damage dealt and your survivability.<br/><br/>
Ensure you have full PvE Power gear equipped. Even Soulbound PvP gear will apply the Bloody debuff.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA attlegrounds1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Queue from Anywhere for Random Battlegrounds!</h1><br/>
<p>Battlegrounds offer team vs team objective based PvP in instanced areas. Engage in Capture the Flag, Point Control, Death Match and more.<br/><br/>
Open the Player vs. Player Tab (Hotkey H). Click Random Battlegrounds and then Join Battle to join the Battleground Queue!<br/><br/>
Queue from anywhere, keep adventuring while you wait, and you'll be returned to your original location after the Battleground ends.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\22_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Accepting Battleground Queues!</h1><br/>
<p>You can continue questing, slaying creatures or explore while you wait for your group to fill up. You will be returned to your original location after the Battleground!<br/><br/>
Your faction emblem will appear on your minimap when you are in the queue. Hover over this icon to see the status and estimated wait time.<br/><br/>
When the Battleground group fills up, you will see a pop-up notification and be teleported to the Battleground immediately.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA attlegrounds3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Cross Faction PvP Against Players Your Level!</h1><br/>
<p>Battlegrounds group players together in level brackets, starting at 10-19, then 20-29 and so on until max level. Max level players are in their own max level bracket.<br/><br/>
Battlegrounds are always cross faction on Ascension. Meaning you will randomly be placed on the Horde or the Alliance side. You can also queue with your friends from the opposite faction.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA attlegrounds2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Battlegrounds Grant Experience. You Can Level Up in PvP!</h1><br/>
<p>You earn Experience for completing objectives, slaying players and completing the Battleground on Ascension. Wins award more experience!<br/><br/>
You will earn experience up to your current level bracket. This means you cannot reach level 20 inside of a 10-19 Battleground. You will still earn an experience bonus at the end of the battleground even if you are max level for that bracket!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA attlegrounds5:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Earn Honor Points, Buy PvP Gear!</h1><br/>
<p>Scoring kills, capturing and defending objectives, and completing Battlegrounds grant you Honor Points that can be spent on PvP Gear!<br/><br/>
Your Honor Points are stored in the Player vs. Player tab (Hotkey H).<br/><br/>
You can store up to 75,000 Honor Points. Honor earned while capped will be lost, so be sure to spend your points on gear, currencies and other prizes from the Honor Quartermaster in your Capital City.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\arenavendor1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Visit an Arena Vendor!</h1><br/>
<p>You can find the Arena Vendor in Capital Cities by the Honor and Arena Quartermasters.<br/><br/>
Talk to Vik "Angry" Smalls or Leeni "Angry" Smalls to view Arena Gear!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\arenavendor2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">No Rating Requirements for Arena Gear!</h1><br/>
<p>Arena gear requires Arena Points to buy. You can earn Arena Points by participating in Arenas!<br/><br/>
This gear does not require a specific Area Rating to buy or equip!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\arenavendor3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Gear Progresses with new Arena Seasons!</h1><br/>
<p>New Arena Gear is released with each new Arena Season! The previous seeason's gear will be available for honor.<br/><br/>
When a new Arena Season starts Arena Points are converted into Honor Points.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\28_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Unlock multiple builds on the same character!</h1><br/>
<p>Unlocking new Specializations allows you to create completely new builds on your same character and freely switch between them!<br/><br/>
You can obtain a |cffe6cc80|Hitem:106954|h[Tome of Specialization II]|h|r from the Auction House, an Honor Vendor, Nozdormu, or the Ascension Shop.<br/><br/>
You can unlock up to 20 specs using Tome of Specialization.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\28_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Swap and Name Specs in Character Advancement!</h1><br/>
<p>You can switch between known specializations in the Specs Tab inside Character Advancement.<br/><br/>
Keep track of your specs by naming them! You can also link an Equipment Set and Enchant Specialization to each spec by clicking the cog wheel.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Ethereal_Bazaar_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">View the Ethereal Bazaar.</h1><br/>
<p>The Ethereal Bazaar sells a limited stock of random Vanity items, spells, and mounts.<br/><br/>
Tiraxis updates his inventory randomly multiple times per day from a pool of thousands of vanity items.<br/><br/>
There is always something new to discover on Tiraxis, and you may even be the first player to find a specific Vanity Item!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Bazaar_Item_Stock:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Each Vanity item in stock can only be bought once!</h1><br/>
<p>When you buy an item from Tiraxis, no one else will be able to acquire that item unless it is randomly selected for his stock again.<br/><br/>
Talk to Tiraxis and purchase any item for Bazaar tokens. You can obtain Bazaar tokens from the Auction House!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\First_Class_Teleporter_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Fast Travel to High-Level Zones and Capital Cities!</h1><br/>
<p>The First Class Experimental Teleporter allows you to air drop between Capital Cities and into high-level zones.<br/><br/>
This Teleporter is located in popular parts of the Capital Cities, it stands out and you won't miss it.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\First_Class_Teleporter_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Steer your Parachute!</h1><br/>
<p>You will be dropped hundreds of yards into the air, don't worry, we provide a parachute that lasts just long enough to get you to the ground... safely!<br/><br/>
You can turn your camera to steer the direction of your parachute. Operator takes full responsibility for their steering!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\wargames1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Wargames Let You Host Battlegrounds and Arenas!</h1><br/>
<p>You can challenge other players or groups to an Arena or Battleground of your choice with Wargames.<br/><br/>
It's up to you how many players to bring! You can enter a wargame 1v1 or bring any group size of your choosing.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\wargames2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Start a Wargame at Teri Glozlik!</h1><br/>
<p>To queue for a Wargame, locate Teri Glozilk in any Capital City.<br/><br/>
Pick the Arena or Battleground you wish to enter. Then type in the name of the other player or group leader you wish to challenge.<br/><br/>
Once they accept, you and your groups will immediately enter the Wargame. No queues!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\36_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Defeat a World Boss! Choose PvE or PvP!</h1><br/>
<p>World Bosses are open world boss encounters that require a Raid to defeat! These bosses respawn on a timer.<br/><br/>
You can challenge bosses in No-Risk PvE mode if you prefer to avoid PvP. Bosses spawn in both No-Risk and High-Risk.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\36_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">World Boss Spawns are Announced in Ascension Chat!</h1><br/>
<p>When a World Boss dies or spawns, it will alert you in the chatbox.<br/><br/>
When looking for a World Boss group, it is easiest to ask for an invite through World Chat.<br/><br/>
You can use the First-Class-Experimental-Teleporter to get a head start on the destination after finding your group.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\36_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">World Boss Take Time to Fully Manifest!</h1><br/>
<p>Sometimes it takes time to travel or fly to a World Boss location.<br/><br/>
Bosses will spawn in an invulnerable state to give the whole raid group time to reach the destination.<br/><br/>
Once the boss fully manifests, it can be engaged!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\36_4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">World Bosses Respawn on Server Restarts!</h1><br/>
<p>Server Restarts have a distinct advantage on Ascension! All World Bosses will respawn as soon as the realm comes back online!<br/><br/>
Logging back in immediately after a restart is a great time to find a Raid Group to challenge each World Boss back to back!<br/><br/>
Keep an eye on Ascension Chat after a restart to find a Raid, or make your own!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\36_5:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Everyone gets loot!</h1><br/>
<p>When a World Boss is killed they will drop a Treasures of Azeroth Cache stuffed with gear that everyone can loot!<br/><br/>
They also drop individual loot that can be rolled on or distributed as your Raid Leader decides.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PathToAscension\InPersonInvasion:2:1}
<p>An invasion is a periodic World Event that spawns throughout Azeroth and scales to how many players are near the zone.</p>

<p>To find an invasion, you can look on your World Map or ask in World Chat if one is currently up.</p>
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PathToAscension\Worldmaplegioninvasion:2:1}
<p>To complete an invasion, you must kill the Final Boss. Once entering an invasion, a percentage completion counter will appear. Once this counter reaches 100% the final boss will appear.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Prestige_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">You can Prestige at Chromie and Redeem Prestige Tokens!</h1><br/>
<p>Chromie offers rewards for prestiges and an in-depth explanation of exactly what occurs when you prestige, including what you keep and what you lose!<br/><br/>
You can find Chromie by the Call Board in your Capital City.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Prestige_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Keep Your Progress. Return to Level 1. Earn Rewards!</h1><br/>
<p>Prestige will reset your character to level 1 and teleport you to your starting zone.<br/><br/>
Prestige is a great way to earn end-game gear, Mystic Enchanting supplies, Marks of Ascension, and more!<br/><br/>
Relive the leveling journey, dungeons, and Battlegrounds with all the knowledge you have acquired, including your saved Mystic Enchants!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Prestige_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Not Starting Over. Starting Better!</h1><br/>
<p>You keep all professions, gear, Marks of Ascension, currencies, Riding Trainer, and items.<br/><br/>
Wildcard and Draft Heroes get to roll a new build! But do not keep the Prestiged Spec's Unspent Hand of Fates or Scroll of Fortune.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA adgesofjustice1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Bosses Drop Badges of Justice!</h1><br/>
<p>Defeat bosses in Heroic dungeons and certain raids to earn Badges of Justice.<br/><br/>
Each boss you conquer rewards you with a Badge, so the more bosses you defeat, the more Badges you collect!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA adgesofjustice2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Spend Badges at G'eras on Gear Upgrades!</h1><br/>
<p>Visit G'eras in Shattrath City to exchange your Badges of Justice for powerful gear upgrades.<br/><br/>
You can find G'eras in the central terrace of Shattrath City, surrounded by other ethereal vendors.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\52_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Mystic Scrolls Contain Powerful Mystic Enchants!</h1><br/>
<p>You can find Mystic Scrolls by defeating enemies, exploring the world, or buying them from the auction house.<br/><br/>
Mystic Scrolls are destroyed on use, but can be used from anywhere!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\52_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Activate Your Mystic Scroll!</h1><br/>
<p>Open the Enchant Scrolls tab by right clicking the scroll in your inventory, or open Character Advancement, Mystic Enchant tab at the bottom, then Enchant Scrolls tab at the top.<br/><br/>
Select Activate to apply the Mystic Enchant from your Mystic Scroll to an Active Enchant Slot.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\52_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Select an Active Mystic Slot!</h1><br/>
<p>After selecting Activate, your Active Enchant Slots will be revealed in the left pane. Select an empty slot to apply your Mystic Enchant to, then hit Save Changes!<br/><br/>
Mystic Enchants are key to unlocking your power as a Hero. Find Mystic Enchants that empower your spells or unlock whole new archetypes to increase your power.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\56_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Rank Up Spells to Increase their Power!</h1><br/>
<p>Higher ranked spells deal more damage and even gain additional effects!<br/><br/>
New ranks become available as you level up.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\56_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Rank Your Spells Up at a Trainer!</h1><br/>
<p>A Beginner's Book of Ascension can rank spells up to level 20!<br/><br/>
Use the Map Lens on your mini-map and select Class Trainer to find a Beginner's Book of Ascension! They can be found near the quest givers in your starter zone and surrounding towns.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\56_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">The Book Icon Lets You Know Spells Can Rank Up!</h1><br/>
<p>The book icon will appear next to spells that can be ranked up in your Spell Book, Character Advancement, and above the menu icon!<br/><br/>
You can train your spells up to max level at a class trainer in your Capital city or anyone's Book of Ascension! Many players have a portable Book of Ascension, so don't hesitate to ask them to summon one!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\60_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Apply a Legendary Enchant to an Active Enchant Slot</h1><br/>
<p>You have 1 Legendary Active Enchant Slot. Selecting a Legendary Mystic Enchant from your Enchant Collection will highlight the center Legendary slot!<br/><br/>
Legendary Enchants grant build defining power! You should always try to have a Legendary Enchant active that empowers your current spells and Archetype.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\60_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Filter for Legendary Enchants!</h1><br/>
<p>You can use the Filter in the top right to quickly find your known Legendary Enchants!<br/><br/>
Select Known, then mouse over Quality and select Legendary.<br/><br/>
You can explore the unknown filter to see everything available!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\61_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Apply 3 Epic Enchants to your Active Enchant Slots</h1><br/>
<p>You have 3 Epic Active Enchant Slots. Selecting an Epic Mystic Enchant from your Enchant Collection will highlight these slots!<br/><br/>
Epic Enchants grant a huge power boost! You should always try to have 3 Epic Enchants active that empower your current spells and Archetype.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\61_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Filter for Epic Enchants!</h1><br/>
<p>You can use the Filter in the top right to quickly find your known Epic Enchants!<br/><br/>
Select Known, then mouse over Quality and select Epic.<br/><br/>
You can explore the unknown filter to see everything available!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Mystic_Enchant_Specializations:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">You start with 2 Enchant Specializations unlocked!</h1><br/>
<p>Enchanting Specializations allow you to create different loadouts for your Active Enchants, allowing you try out different builds without overwriting your current enchants and create loadouts to adapt to specific scenarios.<br/><br/>
You do not need an Altar to swap between Enchanting Specializations! Just open the Mystic Enchant tab from Character Advancement. You can swap anywhere, even in dungeons and raids.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\62_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Unlock Multiple Enchant Specializations!</h1><br/>
<p>Obtain a |cffe6cc80|Hitem:1806961|h[Mystic Enchanting: Specialization]|h|r to unlock more Enchant Specializations!<br/><br/>
These can be obtained from the Auction House, Tiraxis and the Ascension Shop.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\63_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Worldforged Mystic Enchants Cannot Be Traded or Found Reforging.</h1><br/>
<p>Worldforged Mystic Enchants can only be discovered or earned! They cannot be traded or found by reforging. Discover them hidden in the world, by defeating bosses, solving puzzles, and overcoming challenges.<br/><br/>
Many Featured Builds use Worldforged Enchants to complete their Archetype. Reaching max level with those Featured builds will also unlock their Worldforged Mystic Enchants!
</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\worldforged2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Discover Hidden Worldforged Enchants!</h1><br/>
<p>You can filter for Unknown Worldforged Enchants in the Enchant Collection.<br/><br/>
Read the tooltip of undiscovered Worldforged Enchants for clues to locate them! You can also ask other players for hints!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\worldforged3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Discover Clues and Explore!</h1><br/>
<p>Follow the clues and discover a Worldforged Mystic Scroll, or explore the world at your leisure! You are sure to discover them naturally while exploring the world.<br/><br/>
Acquire a Worldforged Mystic Enchant Scroll and Extract it to your Enchant Collection.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PathToAscension\Fullbuild:2:1}
<p>Mystic Enchants add significant power to your build. Being fully enchanted will determine your success in end-game content.</p>

<p>Apply a Mystic Enchant in all 17 Active Enchant Slots.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\74_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Slay Creatures and Complete Quests to Gain Experience!</h1><br/>
<p>Slaying creatures and completing quests is the primary way to gain Experience!<br/><br/>
Your experience bar is located directly above your hot bar and menu bar. You can mouse over it to see the exact amount of experience required to gain your next level.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\reachlevelten2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">NPCs with Yellow Exclamation Points Offer Quests!</h1><br/>
<p>NPCs with a Yellow Exclamation Point offer quests. Complete quests to earn loot and big Experience.<br/><br/>
Completing quests is a great way to get stronger. They can reward gear, |cffe6cc80|Hitem:1297884|h[Adventurer's Cache]|h|r, Reputations, and more!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\74_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Yellow Names are Non-Aggressive. Red Names Attack on Sight!</h1><br/>
<p>Enemies become more dangerous as you level up and venture into more difficult areas. If you’re feeling bold, you can set off on any nearby road. Roads will lead you to new towns and villages with more challenging Quests.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\74_4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">See How Much Experience You Earn!</h1><br/>
<p>You can see the experience gained from slaying creatures and completing quests on screen! More difficult creatures and quests grant more Experience.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\76_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Fast Travel Home with Your Hearthstone!</h1><br/>
<p>Make an Inn your Home at an Innkeeper to set your Hearthstone location, allowing you to teleport back to your home Inn from anywhere in the world.<br/><br/>
Logging out while inside an inn grants you bonus Rested Experience!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\76_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Find Innkeepers in Most Towns!</h1><br/>
<p>Innkeepers have everything you need to rest and relax! They sell Bags, Food, and Drink.<br/><br/>
Innkeepers are found in Cities and most Quest Hubs. You can locate them by using the Map Lens and selecting Innkeeper.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\80_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<p>Continue your journey and acquire enough experience to reach level 15.<br/><br/>
As you continue advancing in levels, you will have to travel to new zones to find more challenging creatures and quests!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\reachlevel152:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Use the World Map to find new zones!</h1><br/>
<p>Hit M, then right-click the map. This will zoom you out to the overall World Map. Mouseover the areas around your current zone. You will see the zone's level range in the top center of the map.<br/><br/>
Find the nearby zone that is level 10+ and travel there to discover new quests and continue your journey to level 15.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\82_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Fly to the Crossroads at the Flightmaster!</h1><br/>
<p>The Flightpath to the Barrens is automatically unlocked! Visit the Flightmaster in your Capital City and fly to a new zone to continue leveling!<br/><br/>
The Crossroads is the most popular quest hub for Heroes leaving the capital for the first time.<br/><br/>
You can find nearby Flightmasters by using the Map Lens and selecting Flightmaster.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\82_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Unlock new Flightpaths at Flightmasters!</h1><br/>
<p>Interacting with a Flightmaster unlocks their Flightpath. Anytime you travel to a new zone, you should look for the Flightmaster’s green “!” in your faction's quest hub.<br/><br/>
Each Flightpath connects to other nearby locations. Unlocking multiple locations allows you to chain them together to fly even greater distances at once! Unlock the nodes between two locations to fly between those locations.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\83_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Fly to Westfall or Redridge at the Flightmaster!</h1><br/>
<p>Nearby Flightpaths are automatically unlocked! Visit the Flightmaster in your Capital City and fly to a new zone to continue leveling!<br/><br/>
Westfall or Redridge are the most popular quest hubs for Heroes leaving the capital for the first time.<br/><br/>
You can find nearby Flightmasters by using the Map Lens and selecting Flightmaster.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\83_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Unlock new Flightpaths at Flightmasters!</h1><br/>
<p>Interacting with a Flightmaster unlocks their Flightpath. Anytime you travel to a new zone, you should look for the Flightmaster’s green “!” in your faction's quest hub.<br/><br/>
Each Flightpath connects to other nearby locations. Unlocking multiple locations allows you to chain them together to fly even greater distances at once! Unlock the nodes between two locations to fly between those locations.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\84_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Continue your journey and reach level 20!</h1><br/>
<p>Continue to accept and complete new quests, venturing into more difficult areas as you gain experience until you reach level 20!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\reachlevel202:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Quests Unlock as Your Level!</h1><br/>
<p>Quest givers with a Grey Exclamation Mark means you must be a higher level to accept their quest.<br/><br/>
As you gain levels, more difficult quests will become available to you.<br/><br/>
Quests in the starter area scale up to level 20! All other quests scale up to max. That means you will never out-level the quests you are on or quest hubs!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\92_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Learned Mounts are stored in your Pets Tab</h1><br/>
<p>•Open up your Character Sheet (Hotkey C).<br/>
•Click the Pets Tab on the bottom.<br/>
•Click the Mounts tab on the top.<br/></p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\92_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Drag your Mount onto your Hot Bars!</h1><br/>
<p>This gives you quick access to summon your mount with a key of your choosing.<br/><br/>
Your first mount increases your movement speed by 40%.<br/><br/>No Riding Training is required. You can learn to ride even faster at a riding trainer.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\93_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Learned Mounts are stored in your Pets Tab</h1><br/>
<p>•Open up your Character Sheet (Hotkey C).<br/>
•Click the Pets Tab on the bottom.<br/>
•Click the Mounts tab on the top.<br/></p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\93_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Drag your Mount onto your Hot Bars!</h1><br/>
<p>This gives you quick access to summon your mount with a key of your choosing.<br/><br/>
Your first mount increases your movement speed by 40%.<br/><br/>No Riding Training is required. You can learn to ride even faster at a riding trainer.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\rerollingspells1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Reroll Unwanted Spells and Abilities!</h1><br/>
<p>|cffe6cc80|Hitem:1101244|h[Scroll of Fortune]|h|r allows you to reroll spells and abilities! Obtain them from Silas Darkmoon.<br/><br/>
Open Character Advancement, find an ability you would like to reroll, and select Unlearn.<br/><br/>
You can always save your Scrolls of Fortune if you like all of your spells and abilities!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\rerollingtalents2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Wildcard Tries to Find Synergy!</h1><br/>
<p>Wildcard isn't always 100% Random! Wildcard will often try to give you a Spells that synergizes with your talents and vice versa.<br/><br/>
Save Spells you want to see synergy for, and reroll Spells you don't want to see synergy for. Wildcard will never stop trying to give you Synergies.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\rerolltalents4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Reroll Strategically!</h1><br/>
<p>Reroll your least-used spells and abilities that are not increasing your build's potential.<br/><br/>
As you continue rerolling the spells that help you the least, you will acquire more and more spells that significantly empower your build.<br/><br/>
This method will ensure you get really strong, really fast! And maximize your Synergy Rolls!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\rerollingtalents1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Reroll Talents!</h1><br/>
<p>|cffe6cc80|Hitem:97933|h[Scroll of Fortune: Talents]|h|r allows you to reroll Talents! Obtain them from Silas Darkmoon.<br/><br/>
Open Character Advancement, find a Talent you would like to reroll, and select Unlearn.<br/><br/>
You can always save your Scrolls of Fortune if you like all of your Talents!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\rerollingtalents2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Wildcard Tries to Find Synergy!</h1><br/>
<p>Wildcard isn't always 100% Random! Wildcard will often try to give you a Talents that synergizes with your Spells and vice versa.<br/><br/>
Save Talents you want to see synergy for, and reroll Talents you don't want to see synergy for. Wildcard will never stop trying to give you Synergies.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\rerollingtalents3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Talents Can Rank Up When Rerolling!</h1><br/>
<p>If you have Rank 1 of a Talent, you can upgrade it to higher ranks when Rerolling other talents! Talent Upgrade Rolls happen randomly.<br/><br/>
Make sure you hang on to lower ranks of talents! Rerolling other talents has a chance to upgrade any of your other talents.<br/><br/>
When you get a Talent Upgrade during a Reroll, you will still Roll into a new talent after receiving the upgraded.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\95_4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Reroll Strategically!</h1><br/>
<p>Focus on rerolling talents that do not directly increase your power or empower your core abilities you use the most!<br/><br/>
As you reroll your weakest or least relevant talents, your build will quickly fill up with talents that all add immense power.<br/><br/>
This method will ensure you get really strong, really fast! And maximize your Synergy Rolls!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\97_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Earn Skill Card Packs from Silas!</h1><br/>
<p>Completing max level Scroll of Fortune quests at Silas grants Sealed Card Packs containing 5 random max-level Talent Skill Cards.<br/><br/>
Use Card Packs from your bags or Skill Cards Menu, then Card Packs and Cards tab.<br/><br/>
Skill Card Packs are found in almost all content. Your Skill Card Collection expands fast!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\97_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Use Your Skill Card Pack to Reveal 5 Cards!</h1><br/>
<p>Each Skill Card Pack contains 5 random max-level Talent Skill Cards.<br/><br/>
Your revealed Skill Cards are automatically added to your Skill Card Collection.<br/><br/>
Your Skill Card Collection is shared across all characters on your account.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\97_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Collect Max-Level Talent Cards!</h1><br/>
<p>Skill Card Packs grant max-level Talent Skill Cards directly.<br/><br/>
Open packs to expand your account-wide collection and give future builds more talent options.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\goldenskillcards1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Buy golden Skill Card Packs from Silas!</h1><br/>
<p>Golden Skill Card Packs contain Golden Skill Cards!<br/><br/>
Talk to Silas, then Select Golden Skill Cards Menu and buy a Golden Pack.<br/><br/>
Then open it from your bags or the Skill Card menu.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\goldenskillcards2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Same As Skill Cards but Golden!</h1><br/>
<p>Golden Skill Cards Packs and Golden Cards function the same as normal Skill Cards, but they can fill the Golden Skill Card slots, allowing even more control of your build as you collect them.<br/><br/>
Golden Skill Cards can only be obtained from Golden Card Packs, or earning enough duplicate cards to earn free packs. They are not found in the world.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\99_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Opening Card Packs Grants Darkmoon Tickets!</h1><br/>
<p>Normal Card Packs grant Darkmoon Tickets and Golden Card Packs grant Golden Darkmoon Tickets.<br/><br/>
Redeem these tickets for specific Skill Cards, Random Uncollected Cards, and Cosmetic Prizes!<br/><br/>
Card Packs always grants tickets, regardless of rarity or duplicate cards.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\99_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Obtain Specific Skill Cards!</h1><br/>
<p>Darkmoon Tickets can be redeemed at Silas Darkmoon to buy Normal, Uncommon, Rare, and Epic Skill Cards. Save up your tickets to acquire key skill cards for your build.<br/><br/>
Talk to Silas, Select the Darkmoon Prizes tab, then Skill Cards or Golden Skill Cards to buy specific cards.<br/><br/>
Normal Tickets grant Normal Skill Cards and Golden Tickets grant Golden Skill Cards.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\99_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Obtain Uncollected Skill Cards!</h1><br/>
<p>Darkmoon Tickets can be redeemed in the Skill Card Menu -> Card Packs tab to acquire 3 random uncollected cards from a specific rarity.<br/><br/>
This is a great option when your Skill Card Collection starts to fill out and ensures you can collect every card!<br/><br/>
Each time you use this option the price increases.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\99_4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Transfer Tickets with |cffe6cc80|Hitem:246095|h[Darkmoon Ticket Pouch (25)]|h|r</h1><br/>
<p>Transfer Tickets between characters on your account with Darkmoon Ticket Pouches.<br/><br/>
Buy a Darkmoon Pouch from Silas! Click Darkmoon Prizes Tab, then the middle Prizes option.<br/><br/>
The Prizes Menu also has exclusive Darkmoon Ticket cosmetics!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\slotaskillcard1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Obtain Skill Cards from Creatures!</h1><br/>
<p>Skill Cards drop from creatures in the World, Dungeons and Manastorm! They can also be found during exploration and solving puzzles.<br/><br/>
Creatures can drop Skill Cards for any spell they cast that can be learned by players. If they cast Divine Shield, they can drop a Divine Shield Skill Card.<br/><br/>
At max level, you can obtain a huge collection of Skill Cards from Silas Darkmoon by completing End-Game Scroll of Fortune quests.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\wildcardslot4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Skill Card Collection</h1><br/>
<p>Open Character Advancement, then click Skill Cards to view your collected cards. Ability and Talent Cards are stored in the tabs at the top.<br/><br/>
You can add Skill Cards to your collection at any time.<br/><br/>
Your Skill Card Collection is shared across all characters on your account, so new characters and Prestiged characters can use cards you have already collected.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\slotaskillcard2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Activate Skill Cards from Levels 1-9!</h1><br/>
<p>Click on the Skill Card you want to slot, then hit Activate!<br/><br/>
Skill Cards can only be activated while you are levels 1-9.<br/><br/>
You are guaranteed to roll any Spell or Talent you have activated with a Skill Card.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\slotaskillcard3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Use Skill Cards Before Your Build Fills Out!</h1><br/>
<p>You will roll any slotted Skill Card Spell or Talent at the first level it is available.<br/><br/>
If you use multiple specializations, you can use Skill Cards in a specialization until that specialization rolls its 5th spell.<br/><br/>
Each Specialization has its own Skill Card slots, so you can experiment with different cards in different Specs.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\105_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Your Tamed Beast has Pet Talents!</h1><br/>
<p>You've gained your first Pet Talent Point! These are earned every 4 levels starting at level 20.<br/><br/>
Right-click your Pet's Portrait, Select Pet Talents, then click any talent to learn it!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\105_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Empower Your Tamed Beast with Pet Talents!</h1><br/>
<p>Each Tamed Beast type has a different Pet Talent tree! Only Tamed Beasts have Pet Talents.<br/><br/>
The Beast Mastery talent located in the Beast Mastery Talent Tree grants an additional 6 Pet Talent Points.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\110_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Travel Faster!</h1><br/>
<p>Mounts greatly increase your movement speed! They can only be used outdoors.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\110_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<p>Seek out a Riding Trainer to receive your first Mount for free!<br/><br/>Select Start Quest and the nearest Riding Trainer will be tracked in your Quest Objectives and as a Yellow ? on the world map.</p>
{page}
