{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Learn_to_Play_Rewards:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Learn to Play! Earn Rewards!</h1><br/>
<p>The Path to Ascension is your guide to Ascension’s custom systems.<br/><br/>
These quests teach you the basics, grant your first free mount at level 6, and let you teleport straight to your Capital City at level 20!<br/><br/>
As you level up, new quests unlock that guide you through Dungeons, Mystic Enchants, Transmog, and more!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\PTA_Supertracker2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Complete Objectives with or without the Quest!</h1><br/>
<p>Each Path to Ascension has a quest that will offer additional guidance with a supertracker marker to direct you where to go.<br/><br/>
You can still complete each objective without the quest. You may even naturally complete objectives just by playing. You still get the rewards!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\120_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Collect Rewards in the UI!</h1><br/>
<p>Return to this UI to claim your rewards once you complete a Path to Ascension quest or objective!<br/><br/>
Make sure to claim your rewards, as they may also unlock new Path to Ascension Quests!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Unlock_New_Quests:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Unlock New Path to Ascension Quests as You Play!</h1><br/>
<p>Level Up and complete Path to Ascension Quests to unlock new ones!<br/><br/>
Continue the Path to Ascension to earn your first free Mount, discover new power through Mystic Enchants, and earn rewards!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\zulgurub1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Zul'Gurub is in Stranglethorn Vale!</h1><br/>
<p>The Zul'Gurub raid located in the north eastern part of Stranglethorn Vale.<br/><br/>
Flying to Booty Bay or using the First-Class Experimental Teleporter to air drop into Booty Bay is a quick way to travel to the raid!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\zulgurub2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Summon Your Raid at the Meeting Stone!</h1><br/>
<p>Use the Meeting Stone to help summon your raid, or accept a summon from other group members!<br/><br/>
The Zul'Gurub Meeting Stone is at the entrance of Zul'Gurub, directly East of Lake Nazferit and North of Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mound.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\zulgurub3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Enter Zul'Gurub</h1><br/>
<p>Head east through the large open gate from the meeting stone.<br/><br/>
Proceed up the stone stairs, and run through the instance portal to enter Zul'Gurub.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\zulgurub4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Defeat Hakkar in Zul'Gurub!</h1><br/>
<p>Hakkar is the final boss of Zul'Gurub.<br/><br/>
In order to defeat Hakkar, you should first defeat the priestesses spread throughout the instance. Each one left alive empowers Hakkar!<br/><br/>
Hakkar is located atop the central temple in the middle of the raid.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\moltencore1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Molten Core is in Blackrock Mountain!</h1><br/>
<p>The Molten Core is inside Blackrock Mountain, located in the north western area of Burning Steppes.<br/><br/>
Flying to Burning Steppes or using the First-Class Experimental Teleporter to air drop into Burning Steppes is a quick way to travel to the raid!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\moltencore2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Summon Your Raid at the Meeting Stone!</h1><br/>
<p>Use the Meeting Stone to help summon your raid, or accept a summon from other group members!<br/><br/>
The Meeting stone is on the center platform held up by giant chains. Enter Blackrock Mountains and run across the chains to reach it!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\moltencore3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Lothos Riftwalker Teleports You into the Molten Core!</h1><br/>
<p>Keep following the path down from the Meeting Stone to find Lothos. Speak to him to teleport into the Molten Core.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\moltencore4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Defeat Ragnaros in Molten Core!</h1><br/>
<p>Ragnaros is the final boss of Molten Core.<br/><br/>
Defeat the bosses throughout the raid before challenging Majordomo Executus. Defeat Majordomo’s minions without slaying Majordomo, and he will surrender and agree to awaken Ragnaros!<br/><br/>
Ragnaros is located in the center of the raid, at the bottom of the lava pit</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\onyxia_classic1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Onyxia's Lair is in Dustwallow Marsh!</h1><br/>
<p>The Onyxia's Lair raid is located in the southern part of Dustwallow Marsh in Kalimdor.<br/><br/>
Flying to Theramore or Mudsprocket in Dustwallow Marsh is a quick way to travel to the raid!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\onyxia_classic2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Summon Your Raid at the Meeting Stone!</h1><br/>
<p>Use the Meeting Stone to help summon your raid, or accept a summon from other group members!<br/><br/>
The Onyxia's Lair Meeting Stone is located just outside the cave entrance in the Wyrmbog area.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\onyxia_classic3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Enter Onyxia's Lair Through the Cave!</h1><br/>
<p>Follow the path into the cave to reach the raid entrance.<br/><br/>
No attunement is required on Ascension.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\onyxia_classic4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Defeat Onyxia in Onyxia's Lair!</h1><br/>
<p>Onyxia is the sole boss of Onyxia's Lair.<br/><br/>
Prepare your raid for a challenging encounter with this powerful dragon!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA wl1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Blackwing Lair is in Blackrock Mountain!</h1><br/>
<p>The Blackwing Lair raid is located at the top of Blackrock Mountain in the Burning Steppes.<br/><br/>
Flying to Burning Steppes or using the First-Class Experimental Teleporter to air drop into Searing Gorge is a quick way to travel to the raid!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA wl2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Summon Your Raid at the Meeting Stone!</h1><br/>
<p>Use the Meeting Stone to help summon your raid, or accept a summon from other group members!<br/><br/>
The Blackwing Lair Meeting Stone is located near the entrance to Upper Blackrock Spire.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA wl3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Cross the Chain and Enter the Balcony.</h1><br/>
<p>From the meeting stone, run across the chain, then follow the rock ledge to the balcony on your right!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA wl4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Enter Blackwing Lair via the Orb of Command!</h1><br/>
<p>After entering the balcony, run down the long hallway and use the orb of command!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA wl5:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Defeat Nefarian in Blackwing Lair!</h1><br/>
<p>Nefarian is the final boss of Blackwing Lair.<br/><br/>
Battle through his minions to confront him at the raid's climax.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\aqr1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj is in Silithus!</h1><br/>
<p>The Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj raid is located in the southern part of Silithus in Kalimdor.<br/><br/>
Flying to Cenarion Hold or using the First-Class Experimental Teleporter to air drop into Silithus is a quick way to travel to the raid!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\aqr2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Summon Your Raid at the Meeting Stone!</h1><br/>
<p>Use the Meeting Stone to help summon your raid, or accept a summon from other group members!<br/><br/>
The Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj Meeting Stone is located outside the entrance to the raid.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\aqr3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Enter Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj Through the Main Gate!</h1><br/>
<p>Walk through the main gate to enter the raid.<br/><br/>
No attunement is required on Ascension.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\aqr4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Defeat Ossirian the Unscarred!</h1><br/>
<p>Ossirian the Unscarred is the final boss of Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj.<br/><br/>
Defeat him to complete the raid!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\aqt1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Temple of Ahn'Qiraj is in Silithus!</h1><br/>
<p>The Temple of Ahn'Qiraj raid is located next to the Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj in Silithus.<br/><br/>
Flying to Cenarion Hold or using the First-Class Experimental Teleporter to air drop into Silithus is a quick way to travel to the raid!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\aqt2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Summon Your Raid at the Meeting Stone!</h1><br/>
<p>Use the Meeting Stone to help summon your raid, or accept a summon from other group members!<br/><br/>
The Temple of Ahn'Qiraj Meeting Stone is located outside the raid entrance.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\aqt3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Enter Temple of Ahn'Qiraj Through the Main Entrance!</h1><br/>
<p>Proceed through the grand entrance to begin the raid.<br/><br/>
No attunement is required on Ascension.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\aqt4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Defeat C'Thun in Temple of Ahn'Qiraj!</h1><br/>
<p>C'Thun is the final boss of the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj.<br/><br/>
Overcome the temple's challenges to face C'Thun at the end.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\naxx1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Naxxramas is in Eastern Plaguelands!</h1><br/>
<p>The Naxxramas raid is located above the Eastern Plaguelands in the Eastern Kingdoms.<br/><br/>
Flying to Light's Hope Chapel or using the First-Class Experimental Teleporter to air drop into Eastern Plaguelands is a quick way to travel to the raid!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\naxx2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Summon Your Raid at the Meeting Stone!</h1><br/>
<p>Use the Meeting Stone to help summon your raid, or accept a summon from other group members!<br/><br/>
The Naxxramas Meeting Stone is located at the base of the necropolis.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\naxx3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Enter Naxxramas via Portal!</h1><br/>
<p>Speak with Archmage Angela Dosantos to enter Naxxramas.<br/><br/>
No attunement is required on Ascension.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\naxx3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Defeat Kel'Thuzad in Naxxramas!</h1><br/>
<p>Kel'Thuzad is the final boss of Naxxramas.<br/><br/>
Battle through the four wings to confront him in the final chamber.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\karazhan1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Karazhan is in Deadwind Pass!</h1><br/>
<p>The Karazhan raid is located in Deadwind Pass in the Eastern Kingdoms.<br/><br/>
Flying to Duskwood or using the First-Class Experimental Teleporter to air drop into Deadwind Pass is a quick way to travel to the raid!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\karazhan2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
