<p>Use the Group Finder ("I" by default) to join Heroic and Mythic TBC Dungeons.<br/><br/>
Defeating bosses in previous raids also offers valuable gear upgrades.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\ilvlsunwell:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Reach Item Level 145 to Enter Sunwell Plateau!</h1><br/>
<p>Work towards an average item level of 145 to prepare for Sunwell Plateau.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\gearup2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Enhance Gear with Call Board Caches and Manastorm!</h1><br/>
<p>Upgrade your equipment by completing Call Board Daily Quests and running Manastorm.<br/><br/>
Call Board Caches adjust to your item level.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\gearup3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Advance Through Mythic+ Dungeons and Previous Raids!</h1><br/>
<p>Participate in Mythic+ TBC Dungeons for higher item level gear.<br/><br/>
Defeating bosses in Black Temple, Battle for Mount Hyjal, or higher difficulties of previous raids provides valuable upgrades.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\219_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Enter The Manastorm from the Dungeon Finder!</h1><br/>
<p>The manastorm is a random, endless dungeon that can be queued solo or with 1-15 players!<br/><br/>
You can join from anywhere by opening the Dungeon Finder menu (Hotkey "i"), and navigating to the Manastorm tab.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\enterthemanastorm2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Dive Deeper for Greater Challenges and Rewards!</h1><br/>
<p>Each boss you defeat will send you deeper into the Manastorm and award Experience, Gear, Gold, Manastorm Caches, Bedlam Bullions, and Bonzo Bolts.<br/><br/>
Millhouse Manastorm will return you safe and sound to your Capital City upon exiting or being defeated.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\228_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Purchase the Hearty Heal Upgrade from Cogsworth!</h1><br/>
<p>Hearty Hearts are a major source of healing in the Manastorm, upgrade them to increase their healing!<br/><br/>
The Hearty Heal Upgrade does not need to be added to your Active Manastorm Spells. It is always active!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\228_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Upgrade Your Most Used Manastorm Spells!</h1><br/>
<p>All Active Manastorm spells can be upgraded up to Rank 10 at Cogsworth! Upgrades can grant increased power, durations, and reduced cooldowns.<br/><br/>
Upgrades are added to your Vanity Collection! All your characters get access to them!<br/><br/>
Make sure to fully upgrade the Active Manastorm spells you use most often.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\231_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Slot 4 Active Manastorm Spells!</h1><br/>
<p>Your Manastorm Active Spell loadout can complement your build! There is no best setup, only the setup that matches your build and playstyle.<br/><br/>
Find a set of Manastorm Spells that complement your build and fill out all 4 slots!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\231_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Cogsley sells new spells and upgrades!</h1><br/>
<p>Cogsley sells many tools that increase your power and offer new utility to allow you to progress further into the Manastorm.<br/><br/>
Once you find a set of spells that work well for you, try to upgrade them as much as possible!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\232_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Slot an Active Manastorm Spell!</h1><br/>
<p>Some Manastorm spells and items must be added to your Active Manastorm Spells to be used.<br/><br/>
From the Manastorm Menu, select an empty Active Manastorm Spell slot and add your |cffe6cc80|Hitem:1300179|h[Millhouse Mobility Mixture]|h|r or |cffe6cc80|Hitem:339050|h[Sprint Serum]|h|r.<br/><br/></p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\232_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Your Manastorm Spells are in your Spell Book!</h1><br/>
<p>Your unlocked Manastorm spells can be found inside the Ascension Manastorm Items tab in your spell book!<br/><br/>
Keep in mind some of these must be added as Active Manastorm Spells to be cast while inside the Manastorm.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\232_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">The |cffe6cc80|Hitem:339041|h[Interrupt Rod]|h|r does not require an Active Slot!</h1><br/>
<p>Some essential spells and items like the |cffe6cc80|Hitem:339041|h[Interrupt Rod]|h|r, |cffe6cc80|Hitem:254041|h[Endless Manastorm Potion]|h|r, and |cffe6cc80|Hitem:254042|h[Milhouse's Magical Escape]|h|r can always be used and do not take up an Active Manastorm Spell slot!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Call_Board_Quests2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Complete Call Board Daily Quests for Gear Upgrades!</h1><br/>
<p>Completing Call Board Quests grants Marks of Ascension, Mystic Orbs, Mystic Runes and a |cffe6cc80|Hitem:978050|h[Callboard Cache]|h|r, allowing you to quickly catch up in gear and jump straight into end-game content!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Call_Board_Quests:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Multiple Quest Completions, One Area!</h1><br/>
<p>Accept all available Call Board Daily Quests! They are meant to be completed together.<br/><br/>
These quests are all located in the same area, allowing you to complete them all without having to travel to multiple zones.<br/><br/>
Be sure to ask to join a group with other players, or invite them to a party you form! Quest progress and items are all shared!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\honorvendoralliance:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Visit the Honor Gear Vendor!</h1><br/>
<p>Visit John "Sailor" Honor in Champion's Hall, Old Town in Stormwind.<br/><br/>
His location is marked on the map with the Honor and Arena Quartermaster POI.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\pvppower2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Honor Gear Boosts your PvP Power!</h1><br/>
<p>This NPC trades PvP Gear for Honor Points!<br/><br/>
You can purchase a full set of Season 0.5 gear after a few Battlegrounds! This gear will massively increase your survivability and damage in Battlegrounds.<br/><br/>
As PvP Seasons progress, new gear will become available in this area.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\honorvendorhorde:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Visit the Honor Gear Vendor!</h1><br/>
<p>Visit John "Sailor" Honor in the Hall of Legends in Orgrimmar.<br/><br/>
His location is marked on the map with the Honor and Arena Quartermaster POI.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\pvppower2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Honor Gear Boosts your PvP Power!</h1><br/>
<p>This NPC trades PvP Gear for Honor Points!<br/><br/>
You can purchase a full set of Season 0.5 gear after a few Battlegrounds! This gear will massively increase your survivability and damage in Battlegrounds.<br/><br/>
As PvP Seasons progress, new gear will become available in this area.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\238_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Earn Free Scrolls of Fortune from Silas Every 10 Levels!</h1><br/>
<p>Scrolls of Fortune (SoF) allow you to reroll spells and talents, rolling off unwanted spells and rolling for stronger talents!<br/><br/>
Visit Silas every 10 levels to claim free Scrolls! You will be offered more and more scrolls every 10 levels.<br/><br/>
Once claimed from Silas, use them in your inventory to add them to your Character Advancement UI.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\238_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Find Silas Darkmoon in your Capital City!</h1><br/>
<p>Silas is marked on your map in Capital Cities with a Darkmoon flag icon.<br/><br/>
Look for Silas and Burth in prominent areas of your Capital! They both have Dice icons floating above their head.<br/><br/>
They can also be found in early level questing hubs.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\scrolloffortune3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Earn Unlimited Scrolls of Fortune at Max Level.</h1><br/>
<p>Silas Darkmoon offers Scrolls of Fortune for Marks of Ascension at max level. There is a cap to how many Scrolls you can claim this way.<br/><br/>
You can earn uncapped Scrolls through Call Board Caches, Dungeons, Battlegrounds, Manastorm, Raids, High-Risk farming and more!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\scrolloffortune4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">There are two types of Scrolls and Multi-Spec Support!</h1><br/>
<p>|cffe6cc80|Hitem:1101244|h[Scroll of Fortune]|h|r allows you to reroll either an Ability or a Talent and |cffe6cc80|Hitem:97933|h[Scroll of Fortune: Talents]|h|r only allow rerolling a Talent.<br/><br/>
Every Specialization has its own unique |cffe6cc80|Hitem:1101244|h[Scroll of Fortune I]|h|r. Every Spec gets free scrolls from Silas while leveling. You don't have to choose which spec to spend your Scrolls on!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\240_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Buy Back Scrolls After Prestige!</h1><br/>
<p>You can buy back Scrolls of Fortune earned from Cases of Fortune and other non-Silas methods.<br/><br/>
Visit Silas Darkmoon and select Repurchase Scrolls.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\240_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Permanent Scroll Progress!</h1><br/>
<p>The Scrolls of Fortune earned from Cases of Fortune and other non-Silas methods can be repurchased every time you Prestige.<br/><br/>
Used and unused Scrolls, bought back or not bought back, are Scrolls are eligible for repurchase! You never lose this progress when Prestiging.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\240_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Silas Scrolls Reset, They Can Not be Repurchased!</h1><br/>
<p>The Scrolls you buy from Silas are not added to your Repurchase Scroll counts. This is because they already reset every prestige!<br/><br/>
The same is true for the bonus scrolls earned each time you Prestige. Those are not added to your Repurchase Scroll counts, you already get them back for free every Prestige.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\241_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Return to Level 1! Reroll Your Build!</h1><br/>
<p>Prestige will reset your character to level 1 and teleport you to your starting zone.<br/><br/>
This will reroll your entire build, unlearning every spell and talent for your current Specialization you prestige in, allowing you to re-level and reroll that specialization.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\241_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Only Reroll Your Current Spec!</h1><br/>
<p>Only your active specialization will be rerolled! Your other Specs will will remain intact.<br/><br/>
While prestiging, all other specs will be locked until you reach max level again.<br/><br/>
This means you can reroll and experiment with multi-specs while preserving your main spec!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\wcprestige3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Permanent Scroll of Fortune Progress!</h1><br/>
<p>Each time you Prestige you will earn bonus Scrolls of Fortune when reaching max level. The amount earned increases every time you prestige!<br/><br/>
You can also buy back Scrolls of Fortune earned from Cases of Fortune, ensuring your time spent farming cases of fortune is never lost.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\241_4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Pick New Skill Cards and Try New Builds!</h1><br/>
<p>Prestige resets your current spec's Skill Cards!<br/><br/>
This allows you to try a whole new skill card loadout and experiment with new found skill cards.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Prestige_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Keep Character Progress. Return to Level 1. Earn Rewards!</h1><br/>
<p>Prestige is a great way to earn end-game gear, Mystic Enchanting supplies, Marks of Ascension, and more!<br/><br/>
Relive the leveling journey, dungeons, and Battlegrounds with all the knowledge you have acquired, including your saved Mystic Enchants!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Prestige_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Not Starting Over. Starting Better!</h1><br/>
<p>You keep all professions, gear, Marks of Ascension, currencies, Riding Trainer, and items.<br/><br/>
Wildcard and Draft Heroes get to roll a new build! But do not keep the Prestiged Spec's Unspent Hand of Fates or Scroll of Fortune.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Prestige_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">You can Prestige at Chromie and Redeem Prestige Tokens!</h1><br/>
<p>Chromie offers rewards for prestiges and an in-depth explanation of exactly what occurs when you prestige, including what you keep and what you lose!<br/><br/>
You can find Chromie by the Call Board in your Capital City.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\242_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Rapid Rerolling is an Optional Way to Roll!</h1><br/>
<p>You can enter Rapid Rerolling through Character Advancement. Click the button in the bottom right.<br/><br/>
Rapid Rerolling only works at max level. You must have already rolled all pending Spell and Talent rolls before you can use it!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\242_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Increases Your Roll Speed, Not Your Roll Chance!</h1><br/>
<p>Rapid Rerolling uses multiple Scrolls of Fortune at once. Each Scroll is still being rolled individually! However, the dice will only stop when they roll a desired spell or talent, or reach the last roll.<br/><br/>
There is no direct benefit to using Rapid Rerolling versus normal Rerolling besides time.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\242_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">You Should Not Always Use Rapid Rerolling!</h1><br/>
<p>Rapid Rerolling is a great tool to help finish builds and quickly roll through large amounts of Scrolls to find a few missing spells or talents.<br/><br/>
If you are still discovering the direction of your build, you should use normal rerolling! This will ensure Rapid Rerolling does not skip over rolls you might otherwise want to explore.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\242_4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Use Suggested Abilities and Talent. Don't Miss Power!</h1><br/>
<p>Suggested Abilities and Talents will tell the dice to stop rolling on spells and talents that may make your build stronger.<br/><br/>
This does not lower your chances to get other Desired entries! It only ensures that the dice don't skip over options that you would gain power from!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\242_5:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">The Dice Stop on Your Desired Spells and Talents!</h1><br/>
<p>Select Spells, Talents or even entire Categories like Mage: Frost or Ability Type: Mobility to tell the dice when to stop rolling.<br/><br/>
Rapid Reroll will skip anything not in your desired! And it will only stop rolling when one of your desired entries comes up.<br/><br/>
If you are rolling 5 scrolls at once, and you get a desired entry on the 3rd roll, it will only use 3 Scrolls before stopping.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\242_6:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Select Spells and Talents To Unlearn!</h1><br/>
<p>Click Spells and Talents to mark them as Undesired.<br/><br/>
Spells that will be unlearned and rerolled will be highlighted in Red.<br/><br/>
Your Locked spells and talents will not appear in this list! Be sure to Lock anything you wish to keep.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\242_7:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Import Full Builds!</h1><br/>
<p>Selecting every possible spell and talent, or category you desire can take time to set up. There is also the chance you miss something!<br/><br/>
You can create a Hero Architect Build, or import a Featured Build specifically designed to optimize Rapid Rerolling.<br/><br/>
Discover how to Import Full Builds from the Path to Ascension Wildcard: Rapid Reroll Full Builds!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\243_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Browse Featured Builds in the Hero Architect!</h1><br/>
<p>Open the Hero Architect to Browse Featured Builds!<br/><br/>
Featured builds are approved builds designed for Rapid Rerolling. These are a great way to jump into end-game build progression and explore new ways to play.<br/><br/>
You can browse builds based on PvE or PvP content, and select one based on your desired role: Tank, Healer, or DPS.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\243_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Core, Optimal, and Empowering Spells and Talents!</h1><br/>
<p>Core Spells and Talents are the bare minimum requirements to use the build.<br/><br/>
Optimal Spells and Talents are the best options for your build. Don't reroll these!<br/><br/>
Empowering Spells and Talents make your build stronger, but are not the strongest option. Reroll these last!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\243_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Import Builds into Rapid Rerolling!</h1><br/>
<p>Select Rapid Roll This Build from the Hero Architect! This will bring you to the Rapid Reroll UI.<br/><br/>
Select Import Hero Architect Build, then select the one you desire from the list.<br/><br/>
Keep in mind that only Featured Builds are guaranteed optimized for Rapid Rerolling. You should inspect community made builds before Rapid Rerolling them!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\243_4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Desire All Spells!</h1><br/>
<p>Click Import Hero Architect build, select your desired build, then click Desire All Spells!<br/><br/>
This will mark all Core, Optimal, and Empowering Spells and Talents as Desired entries. This means the Dice will always stop on spells and talents that empower this chosen build!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\243_5:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Unlearn All Non-Build Spells!</h1><br/>
<p>Click Import Hero Architect build, select your desired build, then click Unlearn All Non-Build Spells!<br/><br/>
This sets all spells and talents you currently know that are not in the build as ones you want to reroll!<br/><br/>
This will not set Locked spells or talents to be rerolled. Be sure to unlock non-build spells you wish to reroll.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\243_6:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">When to Reroll Empowering Spells and Talents!</h1><br/>
<p>As you Rapid Reroll, eventually your entire build will consist of Core, Optimal, and Empowering spells and talents.<br/><br/>
At this point, you can begin marking Empowering Spells and Talents to be unlearned to try to seek out Optimal Spells and Talents!<br/><br/>
You should reroll Empowering entries one at a time to ensure your build retains as much power while rerolling as possible.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\243_7:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Lock Your Build Spells!</h1><br/>
<p>Click Import Hero Architect build, select your desired build, then click Lock Core, Optimal, Empowering Spells!<br/><br/>
Be sure to lock spells in your build to prevent accidentally rerolling them! This is also a great way to see how many spells and talents you have towards your desired build.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\244_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Earn LP by Securing Your Account!</h1><br/>
<p>Visit https://ascension.gg/user/account-overview and secure your account to earn Loyalty Points!<br/><br/>
LP can be spent on soulbound vanity items! Claim 50 LP for securing your account.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\244_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Visit the LP Item Shop!</h1><br/>
<p>Open the Store on the website or the Launcher.<br/><br/>
LP is displayed as the silver currency, you can see your current LP in the top right of the website or launcher.
Open the Store, then click the LP Items category to spend your LP!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\244_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Delivered Straight to Your Mailbox!</h1><br/>
<p>Store items are delivered straight to your mailbox. You can choose which realm and character you want them delivered to when checking out.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\245_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Save Your Equipment’s Appearance with the Wardrobe!</h1><br/>
<p>Your Wardrobe keeps a record of all the equipment your characters collect over the course of your adventure on the server! You can find your Wardrobe by hitting ‘N’, and selecting the Wardrobe tab under Character Advancement.<br/><br/>
Find appearances by looting enemies, purchasing equipment from other players or npcs, and completing quests!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\245_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Gotta Collect Them All!</h1><br/>
<p>To save an item’s appearance to your wardrobe, use Ctrl + Right Click on a piece of gear in your inventory to save its appearance. You can also do this by equipping the item yourself!<br/><br/>
Continue your adventures and collect 10 Transmog Appearances!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\246_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Character Customization Extends to Your Pets!</h1><br/>
<p>As a Hero who can have a pet battling at your side, you have the freedom to customize your pet’s appearance to suit your class fantasy!<br/><br/>
Using the Wardrobe, you can find and preview the appearance of various pets under the “Pet” tab in the upper menus.<br/><br/>
There are 5 different types of tameable pets in Ascension. Click your pet's category using the upper icons to view its cosmetics!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\246_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Pet Cosmetics Can be Found Throughout the World!</h1><br/>
<p>To obtain a new appearance for your pet, you’ll need to find its origin item. You can find this by tracking down the creature in the world and slaying it, or by buying it off another player with the Auction House.<br/><br/>
Every enemy that can be categorized as a pet type, has a chance to drop its pet cosmetic, which you can then loot and learn its appearance with Ctrl + Right Click!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\246_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Use the Wardrobe to Find Your New Pet</h1><br/>
<p>Use the Wardrobe tab under Character Advancement to find your new pet and click Apply.<br/><br/>
This not only changes the appearance of your pet, but also its stats and abilities! Each pet has a different set of spells and style of play, so it’s up to you to find which pet is best for you!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\246_4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Pet Cosmetics are Realm-Wide!</h1><br/>
<p>Pet Cosmetics are also saved under the Vanity tab in Character Advancement.<br/><br/>
If you ever lose your pet or want to use its appearance and abilities on another character, you can have it delivered through Vanity!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\arenavendor1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Visit an Arena Vendor!</h1><br/>
<p>You can find the Arena Vendor in Capital Cities by the Honor and Arena Quartermasters.<br/><br/>
Talk to Vik "Angry" Smalls or Leeni "Angry" Smalls to view Arena Gear!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\arenavendor2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">No Rating Requirements for Arena Gear!</h1><br/>
<p>Arena gear requires Arena Points to buy. You can earn Arena Points by participating in Arenas!<br/><br/>
This gear does not require a specific Area Rating to buy or equip!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\arenavendor3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Gear Progresses with new Arena Seasons!</h1><br/>
<p>New Arena Gear is released with each new Arena Season! The previous seeason's gear will be available for honor.<br/><br/>
When a new Arena Season starts Arena Points are converted into Honor Points.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\pvepower1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">PvE Power Increases Damage, Healing, and Survivability!</h1><br/>
<p>You can view your PvE Power in your Character Sheet.<br/><br/>
PvE Power is only active at max level and is critical to progressing through end-game PvE content on Ascension.<br/><br/>
PvE Power does not affect other players in PvP! It is only active against creatures.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\pvepower2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Gear Obtained from Dungeons and Raids has PvE Power!</h1><br/>
<p>Gear obtained from max level PvE content has PvE power. This includes Bind on Equip gear.<br/><br/>
Acquire a set of PvE gear by queuing for Dungeons, Call Board Daily Quests, The Manastorm, and through the Auction House (just add "pve" to your search).</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\pvepower1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
