Open packs to expand your account-wide collection and give future builds more talent options.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\rapidrerolling1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Rapid Rerolling is an Optional Way to Roll!</h1><br/>
<p>You can enter Rapid Rerolling through Character Advancement. Click the button in the bottom right.<br/><br/>
Rapid Rerolling only works at max level. You must have already rolled all pending Spell and Talent rolls before you can use it!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\rapidrerolling2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Increases Your Roll Speed, Not Your Roll Chance!</h1><br/>
<p>Rapid Rerolling uses multiple Scrolls of Fortune at once. Each Scroll is still being rolled individually! However, the dice will only stop when they roll a desired spell or talent, or reach the last roll.<br/><br/>
There is no direct benefit to using Rapid Rerolling versus normal Rerolling besides time.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\rapidrerolling3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">You Should Not Always Use Rapid Rerolling!</h1><br/>
<p>Rapid Rerolling is a great tool to help finish builds and quickly roll through large amounts of Scrolls to find a few missing spells or talents.<br/><br/>
If you are still discovering the direction of your build, you should use normal rerolling! This will ensure Rapid Rerolling does not skip over rolls you might otherwise want to explore.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\rapidrerolling4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Use Suggested Abilities and Talent. Don't Miss Power!</h1><br/>
<p>Suggested Abilities and Talents will tell the dice to stop rolling on spells and talents that may make your build stronger.<br/><br/>
This does not lower your chances to get other Desired entries! It only ensures that the dice don't skip over options that you would gain power from!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\rapidrerolling5:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">The Dice Stop on Your Desired Spells and Talents!</h1><br/>
<p>Select Spells, Talents or even entire Categories like Mage: Frost or Ability Type: Mobility to tell the dice when to stop rolling.<br/><br/>
Rapid Reroll will skip anything not in your desired! And it will only stop rolling when one of your desired entries comes up.<br/><br/>
If you are rolling 5 scrolls at once, and you get a desired entry on the 3rd roll, it will only use 3 Scrolls before stopping.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\rapidrerolling6:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Select Spells and Talents To Unlearn!</h1><br/>
<p>Click Spells and Talents to mark them as Undesired.<br/><br/>
Spells that will be unlearned and rerolled will be highlighted in Red.<br/><br/>
Your Locked spells and talents will not appear in this list! Be sure to Lock anything you wish to keep.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\rapidrerolling7:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Import Full Builds!</h1><br/>
<p>Selecting every possible spell and talent, or category you desire can take time to set up. There is also the chance you miss something!<br/><br/>
You can create a Hero Architect Build, or import a Featured Build specifically designed to optimize Rapid Rerolling.<br/><br/>
Discover how to Import Full Builds from the Path to Ascension Wildcard: Rapid Reroll Full Builds!</p>

